-- title:
--   Chart functions of the two-chart model: stalks and primes (q=2)
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $q$ is a prime with $q = 2$, $M'$ is a nonzero natural number not divisible by $q$, and $A$ is a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lying over $q$ in the sense that $q$ belongs to the nonunits of $A$. Write $\operatorname{ResidueField} A$ for the residue field of $A$, $\mathcal M_{M'} =$ `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` for the intermediate field of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}(\overline{\mathbb Q})$ obtained by adjoining to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ the coefficientwise images of the $q$-expansions in the full level-$M'$ modular function field, and $\overline F =$ `fieldBar q M'` for the corresponding base change of the function field of level $\Gamma_H(q^2M')$, where $H =$ `levelH q M'` is the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^{\times} \to (\mathbb Z/q)^{\times}$, i.e. the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$. Further, $\mathcal M^{\mathrm c} =$ `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` is the subfield of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}(\operatorname{ResidueField} A)$ generated over the residue field by the reductions of the $q$-expansions of $j$ and of $j$ at level $M'$.
--
--   The reduction data are: a finite set $W$ of places of $\mathcal M^{\mathrm c}$ over $\operatorname{ResidueField} A$, with `hW` saying that $W$ consists exactly of the supersingular places, that is of the places $w$ that are rational, are affine geometric places, and satisfy $w.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of the geometric $j$-generator lies in `ssJSet q (ResidueField A)` (those $j$ for which every elliptic curve of that $j$-invariant has no nonzero $q$-torsion point); the inclusion `hle :`$\mathcal M_{M'} \le \overline F$; a constant reduction $R_0$ of $\mathcal M_{M'}$ to $\mathcal M^{\mathrm c}$ over $A$, i.e. a valuation subring $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ of $\mathcal M_{M'}$, a surjective ring homomorphism $R_0.\mathrm{residue}$ from it onto $\mathcal M^{\mathrm c}$ with kernel the maximal ideal, a map $R_0.\mathrm{placeMap}$ on places, the conditions that $x \in A$ iff its image lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ and that $R_0.\mathrm{residue}$ restricted to $A$ is the residue map of $A$, the scaling property that every nonzero $f$ admits $c$ with $c \cdot f$ integral of nonzero residue, preservation of degrees by $R_0.\mathrm{placeMap}$, and the compatibility of the pushforward of divisors along $R_0.\mathrm{placeMap}$ with orders of residues; and the hypothesis `hR₀`, that for every Laurent series $y$ with coefficients in $A$ whose image in $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}(\overline{\mathbb Q})$ lies in $\mathcal M_{M'}$, that image lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ and its $R_0$-residue, read as a Laurent series over $\operatorname{ResidueField} A$, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$. Finally $\zeta$ is a primitive $q$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ (an element of `Idx q`).
--
--   The Igusa data consist of a family $O^{\mathrm{Ig}}$ of valuation subrings of $\overline F$ indexed by $\mathbb P^1(\mathbb Z/q)$, subject to: `hIg_inf`, describing $O^{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$ at the point $[1:0]$ as the set of $f$ for which there are Laurent series $x, y$ with coefficients in $A$, the reduction of $y$ nonzero, and $f \cdot y = x$; `hIg`, that every $\ell \in \mathbb P^1(\mathbb Z/q)$ is $\mathrm{redQ}(\gamma) \cdot [1:0]$ for some $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ with $O^{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell)$ the preimage of $O^{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$ under `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ`; `hIg_inj`, injectivity of $O^{\mathrm{Ig}}$; and `hIg_perm`, that for every primitive $q$-th root $\zeta'$ and every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ the preimages of the $O^{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell)$ under `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` permute the family.
--
--   The supersingular data consist of a family $O^{\mathrm{SS}}$ of valuation subrings of $\overline F$ indexed by $W$, subject to: `hSS_A`, that for $x \in \overline{\mathbb Q}$ the image of $x$ lies in $O^{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ iff $x \in A$; `hSS_over`, that for $s \in W$ and $f \in R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ which has non-negative order at every place of $\mathcal M_{M'}$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ at which the base-changed $q$-expansion `jq` of $j$ has non-negative order, and whose $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation subring of the place $s$, the image of $f$ in $\overline F$ lies in $O^{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ and, for every $a \in A$ whose residue in $\operatorname{ResidueField} A$ equals $s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of that residue of $f$, the difference of the image of $f$ and the image of $a$ lies in $O^{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ and in its maximal ideal; `hSS_fix`, that each $O^{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ is its own preimage under every `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$; and `hSS_tr`, that each $O^{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ contains an element $t$ such that $t$ minus the image of any $a \in A$ lies in $O^{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ and is a unit there. In addition $R$ is a regular prolongation of $\overline F$ to `xHFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) (q ^ 2 * M') (levelH q M')` over $A$ — a valuation subring $R.\mathrm{integers}$ with a surjective residue homomorphism onto that characteristic-$q$ level field whose kernel is the maximal ideal, compatible with $A$ and with the residue map of $A$, and satisfying the same scaling property — with `hR` identifying $R.\mathrm{integers}$ with $O^{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$, and `hR₀O` asserting that $f \in R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ iff its image in $\overline F$ lies in $O^{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$.
--
--   The arithmetic data are: an element $\pi \in A$ with $\pi^{q^2-1} = q$; an intermediate field $k_0$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$ and $\pi_0 \in k_0$ lying in $A$, such that $A \cap k_0$ is a discrete valuation ring (`hdvr`) with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$ (`hunif`), is Henselian (`hhens`) and has algebraically closed residue field (`hres`), together with `hκ`: every $a \in A$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to some element of $k_0$ lying in $A$; a prime $\ell \ge 3$ with $\ell \neq q$ and $\ell \nmid M'$; an element $\zeta_0 \in k_0$ which is a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity; an element $\varpi_t \in k_0 \cap A$ with $\varpi_t^{q^2-1} = q\,u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$; and a finite extension $K_1$ of $k_0$ inside $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ carrying the valuation subring $A_1 = A \cap K_1$ (`hA₁`), which is a discrete valuation ring and Henselian.
--
--   Giving $\overline F$ the $k_0$-algebra structure through $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, the assertion is universally quantified over intermediate fields $F_0$ of $\overline F / k_0$ satisfying four conditions: the join of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ is all of $\overline F$; $F_0$ is stable under every `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$; a linear disjointness condition, namely that for every finite extension $K'$ of $k_0$ in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, every $m$, every $c : \mathrm{Fin}\,m \to \overline{\mathbb Q}$ linearly independent over $K'$ and every $a : \mathrm{Fin}\,m \to \overline F$ with all $a_i$ in the join of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $K'$, the relation $\sum_i c_i a_i = 0$ forces all $a_i = 0$; and that every element of $\overline F$ whose underlying Laurent series has rational coefficients (lies in the range of `coeffEmb`) belongs to $F_0$.
--
--   Write $\mathcal E_1$ for the join of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield of $\overline F$ generated by the image of $K_1$. The assertion is further quantified over an $A_1$-algebra structure on $\mathcal E_1$ whose structure map agrees on $A_1$ with the inclusion $K_1 \subseteq \overline{\mathbb Q} \to \overline F$, and over an element $j_1 \in \mathcal E_1$, nonzero, whose image in $\overline F$ is the inclusion along `hle` of the base-changed $q$-expansion `jq` of $j$.
--
--   Let $\mathfrak X =$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236) $A_1\,\mathcal E_1\,j_1$, the pushout of the two morphisms from the middle scheme to $X_{\mathrm{fin}} = \operatorname{Spec}$ of the algebra of elements of $\mathcal E_1$ integral over $A_1[j_1]$ and to $X_{\infty} = \operatorname{Spec}$ of the algebra of elements integral over $A_1[j_1^{-1}]$, with structural morphisms $\iota_{\mathrm{fin}}$ and $\iota_{\infty}$. Two predicates on points $x$ of $\mathfrak X$ and elements $f \in \mathcal E_1$ are introduced: $\mathrm{InStalk}(x, f)$ holds when for every point $y$ of $X_{\mathrm{fin}}$ with $\iota_{\mathrm{fin}}$-image $x$ there are $g, h$ in the finite chart algebra with $h \notin y.\mathrm{asIdeal}$ and $f h = g$ in $\mathcal E_1$, and likewise for every point $y$ of $X_{\infty}$ with $\iota_{\infty}$-image $x$, using the chart algebra at infinity; $\mathrm{InMax}(x, f)$ is the same with the extra requirement $g \in y.\mathrm{asIdeal}$ in each clause. The statement also introduces two further abbreviations, $\mathrm{Centred}$ (a place $P$ of $\overline F$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ is rational and, for every $f$ with $\mathrm{InStalk}(x, f)$, $f$ lies in the valuation subring of $P$, $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f) \in A$, and the $A$-valuation of $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f)$ is $< 1$ exactly when $\mathrm{InMax}(x, f)$) and $\mathrm{GoodPt}$ (the point lies over the closed point of $\operatorname{Spec} A_1$, is closed, every chart function whose image lies in the nonunits of $R.\mathrm{integers}$ lies in the prime of each chart point above it, and for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism from the finite chart algebra to $\Omega$ with kernel the prime of a point of $X_{\mathrm{fin}}$ above it, the image of $j_1$ avoids `ssJSet q Ω`); neither occurs in the conclusion.
--
--   The conclusion is the conjunction of two clauses. First: for every point $y$ of $X_{\mathrm{fin}}$ and every element $b$ of the finite chart algebra, $\mathrm{InStalk}$ holds at the $\iota_{\mathrm{fin}}$-image of $y$ for the image of $b$ in $\mathcal E_1$, and $\mathrm{InMax}$ holds there for the image of $b$ if and only if $b \in y.\mathrm{asIdeal}$. Second: for every point $y$ of $X_{\infty}$ and every element $b$ of the chart algebra at infinity, $\mathrm{InStalk}$ holds at the $\iota_{\infty}$-image of $y$ for the image of $b$, and $\mathrm{InMax}$ holds there for the image of $b$ if and only if $b \in y.\mathrm{asIdeal}$.
--
--   This is the chart dictionary for the two-chart integral model of the level field: a function coming from a chart algebra lies in the stalk at every point of the model below one of its chart points, and it lies in the maximal ideal there precisely when it belongs to the prime of that chart point; it is the $q = 2$ instance, stated inside the frame of the Igusa and supersingular covering data of the level field. It is used in the subsequent analysis of that model — in centring places of $\overline F$ on the model after a level automorphism, in producing étale coordinates on stalks at points read off the model, and in showing that the $j$-value at a centred point avoids the supersingular locus.
